1
00:00:07,625 --> 00:00:09,025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:36,665 --> 00:01:39,025
ADAPTED FROM <i>THE EARLY SPRING</i> ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:01:39,825 --> 00:01:40,665
Good.

4
00:01:41,305 --> 00:01:42,265
Keep it steady.

5
00:01:42,985 --> 00:01:43,985
Not bad.

6
00:01:57,425 --> 00:01:58,265
What are you doing?

7
00:01:59,985 --> 00:02:03,025
Do you just slam on the brakes
and hope you hit the right gear?

8
00:02:03,105 --> 00:02:04,505
Is that how you drive?

9
00:02:05,145 --> 00:02:06,505
Start over.

10
00:02:06,585 --> 00:02:07,905
Put it in gear.

11
00:02:07,985 --> 00:02:09,785
-In gear.
-Here.

12
00:02:09,864 --> 00:02:11,865
Go on. Signal.

13
00:02:12,385 --> 00:02:13,865
Good. Go.

14
00:02:18,585 --> 00:02:20,305
Forget it. Take a break.

15
00:02:20,385 --> 00:02:21,745
Switch drivers. Your turn.

16
00:02:26,345 --> 00:02:27,825
OK. Shift gears. Go.

17
00:02:28,785 --> 00:02:30,705
Good. Turn left.

18
00:02:32,305 --> 00:02:34,665
Good. Turn left.

19
00:02:38,185 --> 00:02:39,545
Stop! Stop, now!

20
00:02:40,945 --> 00:02:43,505
Did they put the wiper switch
in the wrong place?

21
00:02:43,585 --> 00:02:46,185
Should I apologize
to you two on its behalf?

22
00:02:47,065 --> 00:02:49,745
I… I give up on you two.

23
00:02:49,825 --> 00:02:51,185
Unbelievable.

24
00:02:58,585 --> 00:03:02,305
LOVE IS STOLEN CANDY

25
00:03:05,345 --> 00:03:07,865
Luke's in charge now,
and he's bringing the heat.

26
00:03:07,945 --> 00:03:10,105
That meeting was intense.

27
00:03:11,225 --> 00:03:12,745
Cut it.

28
00:03:12,825 --> 00:03:14,425
The overall budget is too high,
and the return is too low.

29
00:03:14,505 --> 00:03:15,505
Cut it.

30
00:03:16,665 --> 00:03:17,825
Cut it. Cut it.

31
00:03:17,905 --> 00:03:19,105
Cut it.

32
00:03:19,185 --> 00:03:21,865
Unless you've thought this through,
my advice

33
00:03:21,945 --> 00:03:23,105
is to cut it.

34
00:03:24,225 --> 00:03:25,345
Every budget got slashed.

35
00:03:25,425 --> 00:03:26,505
Not a cent gets spent.

36
00:03:27,545 --> 00:03:29,705
Clear goals, solid action plans,

37
00:03:29,785 --> 00:03:32,425
and every expense fully accounted for.
I learned a lot again.

38
00:03:33,905 --> 00:03:35,705
But I think Luke might have made

39
00:03:35,785 --> 00:03:38,585
a lot of enemies in that meeting.

40
00:03:38,665 --> 00:03:41,105
He's not worried, so why are you?

41
00:03:41,185 --> 00:03:42,705
He doesn't care at all.

42
00:03:42,785 --> 00:03:44,265
He's so brutally direct.

43
00:03:44,345 --> 00:03:46,585
-It's so sexy.
-I'm telling you,

44
00:03:46,665 --> 00:03:49,865
those old fogies
needed to be put in their place.

45
00:03:49,945 --> 00:03:51,745
They spent money like water,

46
00:03:51,825 --> 00:03:53,425
then dragged their feet during audits.

47
00:03:53,505 --> 00:03:57,105
I think I understand why the board
put Luke in charge.

48
00:03:58,505 --> 00:03:59,785
Who else could do it?

49
00:03:59,865 --> 00:04:03,385
Just like you said,
that's this stubborn mule's…

50
00:04:03,465 --> 00:04:05,745
Irresistible charm.

51
00:04:07,905 --> 00:04:09,265
Tell me.

52
00:04:09,345 --> 00:04:12,185
-Have you lost your mind?
-Me?

53
00:04:12,265 --> 00:04:14,305
You must have,
taking on that basketball game.

54
00:04:14,385 --> 00:04:16,504
It's a thankless job.

55
00:04:16,585 --> 00:04:19,145
Actually, I've realized
that to move a project forward,

56
00:04:19,225 --> 00:04:21,785
you need to get everyone
in the internal process on board.

57
00:04:21,865 --> 00:04:25,505
This gives me a chance
to get to know people in every department.

58
00:04:26,425 --> 00:04:29,425
Things are always easier
when people know you.

59
00:04:30,905 --> 00:04:33,585
Not bad, Shang Zhitao.

60
00:04:33,665 --> 00:04:35,905
You've got a strategy.
I underestimated you.

61
00:04:36,785 --> 00:04:37,705
I'll do my best.

62
00:04:39,545 --> 00:04:40,585
Eat more meat.

63
00:04:40,665 --> 00:04:43,265
Get some vitamins and protein in you.

64
00:04:43,945 --> 00:04:46,145
Let's see whether
you're still smiling in a few days.

65
00:05:00,345 --> 00:05:01,225
Tao.

66
00:05:02,025 --> 00:05:02,945
Was that Flora?

67
00:05:03,865 --> 00:05:05,225
Why did she run off so fast?

68
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:06,785
Luke. Tracy.

69
00:05:08,505 --> 00:05:10,425
Maybe she thinks we're terrifying.

70
00:05:11,025 --> 00:05:12,305
Not us.

71
00:05:12,385 --> 00:05:13,505
Probably just you.

72
00:05:15,825 --> 00:05:17,825
But Flora really is impressive.

73
00:05:18,425 --> 00:05:20,465
She's diligent and dependable.

74
00:05:21,545 --> 00:05:22,985
I like her.

75
00:05:24,825 --> 00:05:25,945
Let's go.

76
00:05:37,745 --> 00:05:38,985
Oh my.

77
00:05:39,065 --> 00:05:40,385
You didn't have to bring
this yourself, Mr. Luan.

78
00:05:40,465 --> 00:05:41,305
Don't mention it.

79
00:05:56,385 --> 00:05:58,105
I know it's hard for your team
to rein in spending,

80
00:05:59,145 --> 00:06:03,185
but I want you to understand
that I'm doing you a favor here.

81
00:06:06,265 --> 00:06:07,545
I've heard.

82
00:06:07,625 --> 00:06:10,145
Headquarters is being especially strict
about budgets this year.

83
00:06:11,425 --> 00:06:12,265
Yes.

84
00:06:13,625 --> 00:06:15,665
Mr. Lin's annual review is still ongoing,

85
00:06:16,865 --> 00:06:18,905
and several of last year's budgets
still haven't been approved.

86
00:06:19,585 --> 00:06:22,185
If they're investigated, the lightest
punishment is a formal warning.

87
00:06:22,865 --> 00:06:24,025
Worse, someone could be fired.

88
00:06:24,105 --> 00:06:27,625
And in serious cases,
criminal charges are possible.

89
00:06:32,065 --> 00:06:34,385
You're in charge
of Lime's biggest project next year.

90
00:06:35,265 --> 00:06:38,265
Keep the budget under control,
and no one can pin anything on you.

91
00:06:41,745 --> 00:06:44,745
I knew you weren't trying
to put me in my place.

92
00:06:44,825 --> 00:06:46,745
I should thank you
for playing bad cop for me.

93
00:06:48,345 --> 00:06:49,505
After all these years,

94
00:06:49,585 --> 00:06:50,665
we know each other well.

95
00:06:51,305 --> 00:06:54,305
After all, we've both
done plenty of scheming

96
00:06:54,385 --> 00:06:55,865
behind each other's backs.

97
00:06:58,385 --> 00:06:59,665
Neither of us would back down.

98
00:07:03,665 --> 00:07:05,585
That was…

99
00:07:06,145 --> 00:07:07,425
my fault.

100
00:07:07,505 --> 00:07:09,345
I like trying to be clever.

101
00:07:09,425 --> 00:07:11,185
What was I thinking,
trying to outsmart you?

102
00:07:11,785 --> 00:07:15,145
All right. From now on,
you've got my full cooperation.

103
00:07:16,985 --> 00:07:19,105
Then let's put the past behind us.

104
00:07:19,945 --> 00:07:20,945
Agreed.

105
00:07:22,545 --> 00:07:23,745
But there's one small thing.

106
00:07:24,425 --> 00:07:27,225
Do we really have to hold
that basketball game?

107
00:07:27,745 --> 00:07:29,105
There's barely any budget.

108
00:07:29,185 --> 00:07:30,745
If we win, we offend the client.

109
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:32,825
If we lose, Lime loses face.

110
00:07:32,905 --> 00:07:34,065
A game is a game.

111
00:07:34,145 --> 00:07:35,265
Winning and losing are part of it.

112
00:07:35,985 --> 00:07:39,705
Giving it your all
is the best way to respect a friend.

113
00:07:41,145 --> 00:07:42,025
That's why you're the boss.

114
00:07:43,625 --> 00:07:44,625
You always see the big picture.

115
00:07:48,065 --> 00:07:51,305
A basketball game for 60 people
on a 5,000-yuan budget?

116
00:07:53,385 --> 00:07:54,505
Did today's meeting mean nothing to you?

117
00:07:55,105 --> 00:07:56,545
What did I say?

118
00:07:57,305 --> 00:08:00,185
If you haven't thought it through, cut it.

119
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:02,665
Keep the budget tight.

120
00:08:02,745 --> 00:08:06,465
This game doesn't count
toward our workload or our team's KPI.

121
00:08:06,545 --> 00:08:09,745
I carved that 5,000 yuan
out of my own budget for you.

122
00:08:11,425 --> 00:08:12,265
Just do what you can.

123
00:08:12,345 --> 00:08:13,465
Whatever you manage is fine.

124
00:08:21,065 --> 00:08:22,345
Dinner's ready.

125
00:08:23,065 --> 00:08:24,305
Tao.

126
00:08:24,385 --> 00:08:26,345
To celebrate Tao's promotion,

127
00:08:26,425 --> 00:08:28,305
we're having something special tonight.

128
00:08:28,385 --> 00:08:30,505
Thanks, Zhu. I still have some work to do.
You guys eat first.

129
00:08:30,585 --> 00:08:32,105
No rush. We'll wait.

130
00:08:33,185 --> 00:08:34,345
I'll check and get back to you.

131
00:08:34,425 --> 00:08:37,225
Dongxiang lamb, simply boiled.

132
00:08:37,305 --> 00:08:38,865
It smells amazing.

133
00:08:38,945 --> 00:08:41,585
The lamb practically melts in your mouth.

134
00:08:41,664 --> 00:08:43,024
-My mom sent it.
-Give your mom my regards.

135
00:08:43,105 --> 00:08:44,305
Tao.

136
00:08:44,985 --> 00:08:46,105
Come eat.

137
00:08:47,105 --> 00:08:49,945
Hello. How much would it cost
to rent your venue?

138
00:08:51,585 --> 00:08:53,785
That much? All right.

139
00:08:54,385 --> 00:08:57,145
Did she get on her boss's bad side?

140
00:08:57,225 --> 00:08:58,705
-Why is she doing grunt work?
-Hello.

141
00:08:58,785 --> 00:09:02,065
I was wondering
if you could offer us a better rate.

142
00:09:03,185 --> 00:09:04,225
All right.

143
00:09:04,745 --> 00:09:05,745
Thank you.

144
00:09:09,705 --> 00:09:11,665
Tao. Come eat first, before it gets cold.

145
00:09:12,425 --> 00:09:13,265
Come on.

146
00:09:22,545 --> 00:09:25,185
Our poor girl's worn out.

147
00:09:25,905 --> 00:09:26,945
Have some meat first.

148
00:09:27,505 --> 00:09:28,705
Build your strength back up.

149
00:09:28,785 --> 00:09:29,945
Eat first.

150
00:09:30,025 --> 00:09:31,505
Have some water spinach.

151
00:09:31,585 --> 00:09:33,865
It might help you work things out.

152
00:09:33,945 --> 00:09:35,865
I'm not hungry.

153
00:09:35,945 --> 00:09:38,745
Why am I under so much more pressure
after getting promoted?

154
00:09:38,825 --> 00:09:40,385
They only gave me a 5,000-yuan budget.

155
00:09:40,465 --> 00:09:43,745
I need to rent a venue, buy jerseys,
and prepare gifts.

156
00:09:43,825 --> 00:09:46,065
That's not even counting transportation,

157
00:09:46,145 --> 00:09:47,825
energy bars, and bottled water.

158
00:09:47,905 --> 00:09:49,145
Your boss has gone too far.

159
00:09:50,465 --> 00:09:53,065
As a seasoned event planner
who does this every day,

160
00:09:53,145 --> 00:09:55,225
I can tell you with complete confidence

161
00:09:56,145 --> 00:09:57,265
that with the budget your boss gave you,

162
00:09:57,345 --> 00:09:59,745
you'd be better off holding up a sign
and begging on the street.

163
00:10:01,345 --> 00:10:04,985
You might even meet a couple of kind souls
who'll toss you a few coins.

164
00:10:11,265 --> 00:10:12,345
That's it!

165
00:10:12,425 --> 00:10:13,465
Why didn't I think of that?

166
00:10:15,225 --> 00:10:16,465
Are you really going begging?

167
00:10:16,545 --> 00:10:19,945
In advertising, we call begging
securing sponsorships.

168
00:10:28,225 --> 00:10:31,185
Mr. Liu, this is Flora from Lime.

169
00:10:31,865 --> 00:10:34,665
I'm calling because Yueteng and Lime

170
00:10:34,745 --> 00:10:36,865
are planning a friendly basketball game,

171
00:10:36,945 --> 00:10:39,945
and we'd like
some of our top suppliers to join us.

172
00:10:40,625 --> 00:10:43,625
I remember your venue
has an indoor basketball court, right?

173
00:10:44,585 --> 00:10:46,425
No… We couldn't possibly.

174
00:11:02,425 --> 00:11:05,905
Our Ms. Shang is really going places.

175
00:11:07,465 --> 00:11:08,305
Good for her.

176
00:11:08,385 --> 00:11:09,945
If I had someone
like Shang Zhitao on my team,

177
00:11:10,025 --> 00:11:11,145
I'd be smiling in my sleep.

178
00:11:13,065 --> 00:11:14,625
She's always been amazing.

179
00:11:27,825 --> 00:11:28,665
Come in.

180
00:11:33,145 --> 00:11:34,185
Boss,

181
00:11:34,265 --> 00:11:37,865
could you spare
some of your valuable time this afternoon

182
00:11:37,945 --> 00:11:39,665
to grace the basketball game
with your presence?

183
00:11:40,945 --> 00:11:42,105
I never attend events like that.

184
00:11:43,665 --> 00:11:47,905
Then may I take the afternoon off
to cheer on our athletes?

185
00:11:53,185 --> 00:11:54,545
What help would you be?

186
00:11:55,305 --> 00:11:56,945
You're just looking for an excuse
to skip work.

187
00:11:58,745 --> 00:12:01,585
Shang Zhitao is my prized mentee.

188
00:12:01,665 --> 00:12:03,705
I should at least be there to support her.

189
00:12:04,465 --> 00:12:06,705
She's really come into her own.

190
00:12:06,785 --> 00:12:10,705
She organized the whole basketball game
without spending a cent.

191
00:12:10,785 --> 00:12:13,625
From jerseys and the venue
to food, drinks, and everything else,

192
00:12:13,705 --> 00:12:15,385
she found sponsors for it all.

193
00:12:15,905 --> 00:12:17,705
She's put together quite an event.

194
00:12:17,785 --> 00:12:19,505
Where did she find the sponsors?

195
00:12:19,585 --> 00:12:22,585
She offered suppliers priority
consideration for the next three years

196
00:12:22,665 --> 00:12:25,945
and got them competing
for sponsorship slots.

197
00:12:26,905 --> 00:12:28,385
Pretty clever, isn't she?

198
00:12:29,145 --> 00:12:30,145
Not bad.

199
00:12:31,625 --> 00:12:32,665
In that case,

200
00:12:32,745 --> 00:12:37,105
use this opportunity to see firsthand
how cooperative our suppliers are.

201
00:12:37,745 --> 00:12:40,225
So I am going there for work.

202
00:12:40,985 --> 00:12:41,865
Give me a break.

203
00:12:42,705 --> 00:12:44,985
Go before I change my mind.

204
00:12:45,065 --> 00:12:45,905
You got it.

205
00:12:46,425 --> 00:12:47,425
Lumi.

206
00:12:47,505 --> 00:12:48,825
Nice new hairstyle.

207
00:12:50,505 --> 00:12:51,625
I know.

208
00:12:52,185 --> 00:12:53,025
Looking sharp yourself.

209
00:12:58,705 --> 00:13:02,665
YUETENG

210
00:13:02,745 --> 00:13:04,625
Jack, how's everything?

211
00:13:04,705 --> 00:13:07,385
The jerseys have arrived. Take a look.

212
00:13:07,465 --> 00:13:09,105
OK. Thanks for your hard work.

213
00:13:09,185 --> 00:13:10,025
No problem.

214
00:13:11,825 --> 00:13:13,705
-These look good.
-They do.

215
00:13:13,785 --> 00:13:15,105
-And here's another one.
-Great.

216
00:13:17,385 --> 00:13:19,505
-Shang Zhitao.
-Lumi.

217
00:13:19,585 --> 00:13:20,865
Not bad.

218
00:13:21,585 --> 00:13:24,305
You've got everything
running like clockwork.

219
00:13:24,385 --> 00:13:25,305
You've finally put your knack

220
00:13:25,385 --> 00:13:28,345
for playing capitalists at their own game
to good use.

221
00:13:28,425 --> 00:13:29,985
I learned from the best.

222
00:13:30,065 --> 00:13:32,265
You taught me that working hard alone
gets you nowhere at Lime.

223
00:13:32,345 --> 00:13:33,705
Flatterer.

224
00:13:33,785 --> 00:13:35,425
I couldn't have pulled this off.

225
00:13:35,505 --> 00:13:37,865
Even those penny-pinchers in Finance

226
00:13:37,945 --> 00:13:40,345
praised how well
you controlled the budget.

227
00:13:41,145 --> 00:13:43,105
Check out the fabric. What do you think?

228
00:13:43,185 --> 00:13:44,105
It's pretty good, right?

229
00:13:44,185 --> 00:13:47,185
The players will look great in these.

230
00:13:51,145 --> 00:13:52,825
A little something for you.

231
00:13:52,905 --> 00:13:53,825
With your new promotion,

232
00:13:53,905 --> 00:13:56,625
you'll want to make a splash
inside and outside the company.

233
00:14:00,025 --> 00:14:03,825
I appreciate the gesture,
but I make it a rule not to accept gifts.

234
00:14:06,345 --> 00:14:07,745
Mr. Luan, here's the thing.

235
00:14:07,825 --> 00:14:11,105
I know Lime created
a new supplier database for our project.

236
00:14:11,185 --> 00:14:14,705
I know several reliable suppliers
I've worked with for years.

237
00:14:15,825 --> 00:14:19,505
They're much easier to work with.

238
00:14:19,585 --> 00:14:22,945
Could you add them to the database?

239
00:14:26,425 --> 00:14:28,865
We'd be happy to consider them.
Send me their information.

240
00:14:28,945 --> 00:14:31,705
As long as they meet
our supplier database criteria

241
00:14:32,265 --> 00:14:34,705
and pass the compliance review,
they can be added.

242
00:14:35,265 --> 00:14:38,745
But if they don't qualify,
no one gets special treatment.

243
00:14:40,505 --> 00:14:44,225
That's why I've come
to discuss it with you, Mr. Luan.

244
00:14:44,745 --> 00:14:45,825
Make an exception.

245
00:14:45,905 --> 00:14:46,945
It's no big deal.

246
00:14:49,185 --> 00:14:53,825
Mr. Wan, Lime has
a very strict evaluation system.

247
00:14:53,905 --> 00:14:56,345
Companies admitted
to our supplier database

248
00:14:56,425 --> 00:14:58,305
must not only be easy to work with

249
00:14:58,385 --> 00:14:59,465
but also highly professional.

250
00:15:00,585 --> 00:15:03,385
We place great importance
on our future collaboration with Yueteng.

251
00:15:03,465 --> 00:15:07,665
We established this supplier system
precisely to avoid the mistakes

252
00:15:07,745 --> 00:15:10,345
that Chengbiao made
when working with Yueteng.

253
00:15:10,425 --> 00:15:13,025
So you see, if I make an exception,

254
00:15:13,945 --> 00:15:15,185
how can I expect others
to follow the rules?

255
00:15:18,985 --> 00:15:21,385
I didn't expect you
to be such a man of principle.

256
00:15:21,985 --> 00:15:23,185
You can still keep the gift.

257
00:15:23,985 --> 00:15:25,025
I truly appreciate it.

258
00:15:26,345 --> 00:15:27,345
We'll have opportunities in the future.

259
00:15:28,585 --> 00:15:30,585
All right. We'll discuss it another time.

260
00:15:30,665 --> 00:15:31,865
I'll be going, then.

261
00:15:36,705 --> 00:15:37,545
I'll see you out.

262
00:15:54,225 --> 00:15:54,905
LU MI

263
00:15:54,985 --> 00:15:56,705
<i>Luke, we won.</i>

264
00:15:56,785 --> 00:15:58,185
<i>Lime won!</i>

265
00:15:58,265 --> 00:15:59,345
<i>There's a celebration tonight.</i>

266
00:15:59,425 --> 00:16:01,745
-Come make an appearance.
-<i>I'm not going.</i>

267
00:16:02,425 --> 00:16:05,825
I know you're worried everyone
won't be comfortable around you,

268
00:16:05,905 --> 00:16:07,105
<i>but everyone's in high spirits.</i>

269
00:16:07,185 --> 00:16:09,305
<i>At the celebration,</i>
<i>all our colleagues will be there,</i>

270
00:16:09,385 --> 00:16:10,945
along with Yueteng's executives.

271
00:16:11,025 --> 00:16:12,905
<i>Just stop by and show your face.</i>

272
00:16:12,985 --> 00:16:15,265
I already met Wan Jun today.
I'm not going.

273
00:16:16,025 --> 00:16:18,625
That doesn't mean
you can't come celebrate with everyone.

274
00:16:20,185 --> 00:16:22,625
If he brings up the suppliers
at the banquet,

275
00:16:22,705 --> 00:16:23,665
don't discuss it privately.

276
00:16:23,745 --> 00:16:25,065
<i>Report it to me immediately.</i>

277
00:16:25,145 --> 00:16:26,745
I know what to do.

278
00:16:26,825 --> 00:16:28,265
But we're celebrating tonight.

279
00:16:28,345 --> 00:16:30,105
<i>We'll just drink. No work talk.</i>

280
00:16:30,185 --> 00:16:32,785
Anyway, whatever he says to you,
report it to me right away.

281
00:16:33,705 --> 00:16:36,505
Fine. I'll tell Flora too.

282
00:16:36,585 --> 00:16:39,865
<i>I just saw Wan Jun asking her</i>
<i>about the supplier database criteria.</i>

283
00:16:39,945 --> 00:16:42,985
-She's there too?
-Of course.

284
00:16:43,065 --> 00:16:44,225
She organized the event

285
00:16:44,305 --> 00:16:46,025
-and deserves most of the credit.
-Sure.

286
00:16:46,105 --> 00:16:47,425
-Our athletes
-We should work together sometime.

287
00:16:47,505 --> 00:16:49,345
-even gave her their medals.
-Thank you.

288
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:52,465
<i>Mr. Wan praised her too,</i>
<i>saying she did a great job.</i>

289
00:16:52,545 --> 00:16:53,385
Bye.

290
00:16:55,745 --> 00:16:59,465
Looks like everyone in
the Business Division is an all-rounder.

291
00:16:59,545 --> 00:17:01,225
-Not really.
-Exactly.

292
00:17:01,305 --> 00:17:03,305
Organizing an event this big
is no easy feat.

293
00:17:03,385 --> 00:17:04,745
I'm John from the Commerce Division.

294
00:17:04,825 --> 00:17:07,184
Next time you need sponsors, come to me.

295
00:17:07,265 --> 00:17:08,265
Nice to meet you.

296
00:17:08,345 --> 00:17:09,265
-Bottoms up.
-All right.

297
00:17:09,345 --> 00:17:10,385
Bottoms up for what?

298
00:17:10,464 --> 00:17:11,704
Don't you dare pressure her to drink.

299
00:17:11,785 --> 00:17:13,865
Flora is our division's pride and joy.

300
00:17:13,944 --> 00:17:15,825
Anyone who pressures her answers to me.

301
00:17:15,905 --> 00:17:16,745
Drink with me first.

302
00:17:16,825 --> 00:17:18,025
-All right.
-Got it.

303
00:17:18,105 --> 00:17:19,105
Let's drink together.

304
00:17:19,184 --> 00:17:20,025
Cheers.

305
00:17:21,345 --> 00:17:22,345
We'll get going.

306
00:17:22,424 --> 00:17:23,464
Take it easy on the drinks.

307
00:17:28,265 --> 00:17:31,065
No wonder you keep drinking
without getting drunk.

308
00:17:31,145 --> 00:17:32,905
You've learned a little trick.

309
00:17:32,985 --> 00:17:34,905
I'm just putting
what I learned into practice.

310
00:17:34,985 --> 00:17:36,665
Clever girl.

311
00:17:36,745 --> 00:17:38,825
You did a great job.

312
00:17:38,905 --> 00:17:42,945
Now all those aloof Lime employees
know who you are.

313
00:17:43,025 --> 00:17:43,865
It was nothing.

314
00:17:45,665 --> 00:17:47,545
-I'm doomed.
-Why?

315
00:17:48,505 --> 00:17:51,865
Luan Nian isn't coming.
I'll never live this down.

316
00:17:52,505 --> 00:17:53,705
Luan Nian was supposed to come?

317
00:17:53,785 --> 00:17:55,065
He's not coming.

318
00:17:55,665 --> 00:17:57,465
During the basketball game this afternoon,

319
00:17:57,545 --> 00:18:00,545
I promised the girls in the Media Division

320
00:18:00,625 --> 00:18:04,505
I'd bring Luan Nian
to tonight's celebration.

321
00:18:04,585 --> 00:18:07,505
I've spent the whole afternoon

322
00:18:07,585 --> 00:18:09,345
answering questions about him.

323
00:18:11,305 --> 00:18:14,225
What… What gossip is there about him?

324
00:18:14,905 --> 00:18:16,665
His love life.

325
00:18:17,225 --> 00:18:20,025
He's handsome, rich,
single, and successful.

326
00:18:22,225 --> 00:18:24,305
Of course the girls are interested.

327
00:18:25,065 --> 00:18:30,825
I already promised them
I'd find out about his love life.

328
00:18:30,905 --> 00:18:33,145
If I do, they'll prioritize

329
00:18:33,225 --> 00:18:36,985
all our proposals for the next six months.

330
00:18:38,865 --> 00:18:42,905
Aren't you trading
your boss's privacy for favors?

331
00:18:42,985 --> 00:18:44,305
Don't be ridiculous.

332
00:18:44,905 --> 00:18:46,545
This is work.

333
00:18:46,625 --> 00:18:48,265
And who am I doing it for?

334
00:18:50,785 --> 00:18:55,265
I just don't understand
what there is to ask.

335
00:18:55,345 --> 00:18:57,745
Luan Nian is so cold.

336
00:18:57,825 --> 00:18:59,905
Why is everyone so interested in him?

337
00:19:07,505 --> 00:19:11,865
Tao, why don't you ask him to come?

338
00:19:11,945 --> 00:19:14,745
You seem to know how to handle him.

339
00:19:14,825 --> 00:19:16,145
Me?

340
00:19:16,225 --> 00:19:17,545
No. I can't.

341
00:19:17,625 --> 00:19:18,905
There's no way.

342
00:19:18,985 --> 00:19:20,905
Don't be modest.

343
00:19:20,985 --> 00:19:22,265
Luan Nian is difficult,

344
00:19:22,345 --> 00:19:24,625
but I always feel
you can get through to him.

345
00:19:26,625 --> 00:19:28,385
I've put my reputation on the line.

346
00:19:28,465 --> 00:19:30,745
-Help me out. I'm your mentor, after all.
-I really can't.

347
00:19:45,825 --> 00:19:47,025
He's here.

348
00:19:47,105 --> 00:19:52,065
Next week's Yueteng proposal
depends on tonight.

349
00:19:56,945 --> 00:19:58,025
Hello, Mr. Luan.

350
00:19:58,105 --> 00:20:00,025
Mr. Luan.

351
00:20:00,105 --> 00:20:01,425
Mr. Luan.

352
00:20:02,065 --> 00:20:03,985
No need to be so formal. Relax.

353
00:20:04,585 --> 00:20:05,505
Have fun.

354
00:20:05,585 --> 00:20:06,745
Boss,

355
00:20:06,825 --> 00:20:09,145
your presence really lights up the place.

356
00:20:09,225 --> 00:20:11,625
I've never seen you this enthusiastic
when entertaining clients.

357
00:20:14,025 --> 00:20:16,105
We're all having a drink and unwinding.

358
00:20:16,185 --> 00:20:18,025
Why don't you have one too and loosen up?

359
00:20:18,105 --> 00:20:18,945
I'm perfectly relaxed.

360
00:20:19,785 --> 00:20:20,625
You go ahead and relax.

361
00:20:22,145 --> 00:20:23,185
-Tao.
-Yes?

362
00:20:23,265 --> 00:20:24,465
Fill Mr. Luan's glass.

363
00:20:30,025 --> 00:20:31,145
Mr. Luan.

364
00:20:31,825 --> 00:20:33,025
Welcome.

365
00:20:35,345 --> 00:20:38,305
Tao. You're the star
of tonight's celebration dinner

366
00:20:38,385 --> 00:20:40,305
and the one who made it all happen.

367
00:20:40,385 --> 00:20:41,825
Let's toast Mr. Luan together.

368
00:20:42,465 --> 00:20:43,785
Cheers, Mr. Luan.

369
00:20:44,985 --> 00:20:46,225
Sorry.

370
00:20:46,305 --> 00:20:47,585
I'm driving, so I can't drink.

371
00:20:51,425 --> 00:20:52,865
You're driving? No problem.

372
00:20:52,945 --> 00:20:54,385
Come on, Tao. Let's drink.

373
00:20:55,345 --> 00:20:56,305
You did great.

374
00:21:00,345 --> 00:21:01,905
Well, I'll let you guys talk.

375
00:21:42,945 --> 00:21:44,065
Tao.

376
00:21:45,345 --> 00:21:46,265
Mr. Wan.

377
00:21:48,385 --> 00:21:49,665
Here's the thing.

378
00:21:49,745 --> 00:21:52,985
I know some excellent suppliers.

379
00:21:53,065 --> 00:21:55,225
They're highly capable and very reliable.

380
00:21:55,305 --> 00:21:56,385
So,

381
00:21:57,705 --> 00:21:58,785
I was hoping

382
00:21:59,985 --> 00:22:01,345
you could give me a hint.

383
00:22:02,065 --> 00:22:03,985
What will it take for Mr. Luan

384
00:22:04,865 --> 00:22:06,385
to make it happen?

385
00:22:09,825 --> 00:22:12,025
Mr. Wan, I think you've misunderstood.

386
00:22:13,065 --> 00:22:15,905
Mr. Luan created this supplier system

387
00:22:15,985 --> 00:22:19,385
so that every contract
can withstand public scrutiny.

388
00:22:20,785 --> 00:22:21,825
Excuse me.

389
00:22:22,425 --> 00:22:23,665
I need to use the restroom.

390
00:22:23,745 --> 00:22:24,625
Excuse me.

391
00:22:59,025 --> 00:23:00,145
Have you been avoiding me?

392
00:23:02,065 --> 00:23:03,105
No.

393
00:23:05,385 --> 00:23:06,625
"Tao"?

394
00:23:08,865 --> 00:23:11,465
Only third-rate salespeople
use alcohol to win clients.

395
00:23:13,705 --> 00:23:15,865
The sponsors helped us a lot this time,

396
00:23:15,945 --> 00:23:18,425
and my colleagues have been working
nonstop for over ten days.

397
00:23:18,505 --> 00:23:23,385
Having a drink together afterward
is just part of normal socializing.

398
00:23:23,465 --> 00:23:26,025
Is drinking part of workplace socializing?
Who taught you that?

399
00:23:26,105 --> 00:23:27,345
You did.

400
00:23:27,425 --> 00:23:30,705
You said if I can't handle alcohol,
I shouldn't drink at all.

401
00:23:30,785 --> 00:23:32,425
I wanted to try a little.

402
00:23:32,505 --> 00:23:34,145
Doesn't that count as progress?

403
00:23:34,745 --> 00:23:36,945
You also taught me
not to forget who helped me.

404
00:23:37,025 --> 00:23:39,945
So, of course, I'm grateful
to my clients and colleagues.

405
00:23:40,025 --> 00:23:41,345
I learned from the best.

406
00:23:44,025 --> 00:23:45,425
I supported your work too.

407
00:23:47,225 --> 00:23:49,345
How come you've never
shown me any gratitude?

408
00:24:01,345 --> 00:24:02,385
I have.

409
00:24:04,985 --> 00:24:07,745
Here. A medal. I got it today.

410
00:24:18,865 --> 00:24:19,745
I don't want it.

411
00:24:32,785 --> 00:24:33,825
Keep it.

412
00:24:35,025 --> 00:24:36,625
Let it remind you
not to keep running away.

413
00:24:59,985 --> 00:25:01,705
Running away keeps me safe.

414
00:25:02,425 --> 00:25:03,825
I'm not like you.

415
00:25:04,705 --> 00:25:05,785
I have to think ahead.

416
00:25:08,585 --> 00:25:11,025
Do accidents fit into your plans too?

417
00:25:12,385 --> 00:25:14,465
Was what happened on the mountain
planned too?

418
00:25:18,225 --> 00:25:19,065
No.

419
00:25:23,305 --> 00:25:25,025
Shang Zhitao, you're pretty heartless.

420
00:25:26,185 --> 00:25:27,545
You like me, but you keep holding back.

421
00:25:27,625 --> 00:25:28,665
Isn't that exhausting?

422
00:25:32,785 --> 00:25:34,545
Mr. Luan, I can't lose my job.

423
00:25:36,105 --> 00:25:38,105
The company doesn't allow office romances.

424
00:25:52,225 --> 00:25:53,225
If that bothers you,

425
00:25:54,825 --> 00:25:56,585
we can keep our relationship private.

426
00:26:06,105 --> 00:26:07,105
-Come on.
-Cheers.

427
00:26:07,185 --> 00:26:08,025
-Let's drink.
-Cheers.

428
00:26:08,105 --> 00:26:09,185
Cheers.

429
00:26:09,265 --> 00:26:10,265
Cheers!

430
00:26:12,345 --> 00:26:14,945
Boss, we're celebrating tonight.

431
00:26:15,025 --> 00:26:18,065
On behalf of Lime's female colleagues,

432
00:26:18,585 --> 00:26:20,025
I have a dangerous question for you.

433
00:26:21,025 --> 00:26:24,065
For an eligible bachelor like you,

434
00:26:24,145 --> 00:26:27,265
are you permanently off the market

435
00:26:27,345 --> 00:26:30,545
or just not taking reservations right now?

436
00:26:31,625 --> 00:26:32,465
Answer me!

437
00:26:33,585 --> 00:26:35,425
Is this what you all spend your time on?

438
00:26:35,505 --> 00:26:36,825
We're celebrating tonight.

439
00:26:36,905 --> 00:26:38,705
You can't talk shop at the dinner table.

440
00:26:38,785 --> 00:26:40,305
-Right?
-Exactly.

441
00:26:40,385 --> 00:26:41,345
-Right?
-Yes.

442
00:26:41,425 --> 00:26:42,425
Exactly.

443
00:26:43,465 --> 00:26:46,585
I think we should discuss
next week's proposal

444
00:26:46,665 --> 00:26:48,345
and whether you can submit it early.

445
00:26:49,025 --> 00:26:50,705
Please, don't. We're celebrating tonight.

446
00:26:50,785 --> 00:26:52,705
No KPI talk.

447
00:26:52,785 --> 00:26:53,785
Right, Tao?

448
00:26:59,065 --> 00:26:59,945
Yes.

449
00:27:01,385 --> 00:27:05,025
Luke, they want to ask you…

450
00:27:09,865 --> 00:27:11,465
Go on.

451
00:27:13,145 --> 00:27:14,625
They want

452
00:27:15,705 --> 00:27:19,105
to know whether you have a girlfriend.

453
00:27:22,185 --> 00:27:23,025
Good job.

454
00:27:23,545 --> 00:27:24,385
Answer.

455
00:27:25,785 --> 00:27:28,065
The only things I want to discuss
with you are work and plans.

456
00:27:28,665 --> 00:27:31,745
Whether I have a girlfriend
is none of your business.

457
00:27:32,865 --> 00:27:34,225
We don't accept that answer.

458
00:27:34,305 --> 00:27:36,425
-Just tell us.
-Tell us.

459
00:27:36,505 --> 00:27:38,425
-Tell us.
-Come on.

460
00:27:38,505 --> 00:27:44,145
Tell us.

461
00:27:45,145 --> 00:27:46,265
You really want to know?

462
00:27:46,345 --> 00:27:48,785
-Of course. Tell us.
-Of course.

463
00:27:48,865 --> 00:27:50,105
-Who is she?
-Tell us.

464
00:28:02,345 --> 00:28:03,865
Actually, I've been divorced twice.

465
00:28:04,905 --> 00:28:06,385
I work so hard

466
00:28:07,545 --> 00:28:09,345
because I have two children to support.

467
00:28:13,825 --> 00:28:17,225
Come on. Everyone over there,
raise your glasses!

468
00:28:17,305 --> 00:28:18,265
Come on!

469
00:28:18,345 --> 00:28:20,185
We're celebrating tonight. Cheers!

470
00:28:20,265 --> 00:28:22,945
-That's nice.
-Cheers!

471
00:28:24,065 --> 00:28:25,785
-How many children do you have?
-Two.

472
00:28:25,865 --> 00:28:26,985
Two? You have two as well?

473
00:28:27,065 --> 00:28:28,025
A third one's on the way.

474
00:28:30,425 --> 00:28:33,065
-Are you getting a cab too?
-Yes.

475
00:28:33,145 --> 00:28:35,985
-Then let's share one.
-Sure.

476
00:28:36,065 --> 00:28:37,865
-Let's go together.
-OK.

477
00:28:44,745 --> 00:28:45,905
I'll drive you.

478
00:28:46,825 --> 00:28:48,425
No need. I'm going over there.

479
00:28:51,305 --> 00:28:52,545
You've been drinking.

480
00:28:53,305 --> 00:28:55,705
-I'll drive you.
-Boss.

481
00:28:58,625 --> 00:29:00,065
You're still here.

482
00:29:00,145 --> 00:29:01,545
Perfect. I need your help.

483
00:29:02,225 --> 00:29:03,745
I'm not your boss after work.

484
00:29:03,825 --> 00:29:05,465
Didn't you already leave in a cab?

485
00:29:05,545 --> 00:29:08,825
The driver canceled on me
and won't answer my calls.

486
00:29:08,905 --> 00:29:10,105
You drove here, right?

487
00:29:10,185 --> 00:29:11,265
Could you give me a ride?

488
00:29:11,345 --> 00:29:12,545
Tao's had too much to drink, too.

489
00:29:12,625 --> 00:29:13,985
Give us both a ride.

490
00:29:14,065 --> 00:29:15,705
It's on your way. Come on.

491
00:29:16,705 --> 00:29:18,265
You're the best.

492
00:29:32,905 --> 00:29:34,865
Lumi. Address.

493
00:29:34,945 --> 00:29:37,625
Boss, drop Flora off first
before driving me home.

494
00:29:40,865 --> 00:29:43,745
By order of priority,
your place comes first.

495
00:29:43,825 --> 00:29:45,025
No. Drive her home first.

496
00:29:45,105 --> 00:29:47,905
Her place is on your way. Mine isn't.

497
00:29:48,825 --> 00:29:50,785
Drop me off first, then. Thanks, Luke.

498
00:29:57,265 --> 00:29:59,745
What cologne was Wan Jun wearing?

499
00:29:59,825 --> 00:30:01,145
It was suffocating me.

500
00:30:01,825 --> 00:30:05,065
Tao, why didn't he offer you a ride?

501
00:30:05,145 --> 00:30:07,745
He spent the whole night
trying to impress you.

502
00:30:08,825 --> 00:30:11,585
I… I was just maintaining
a client relationship.

503
00:30:11,665 --> 00:30:13,625
We briefly discussed
some advertising ideas.

504
00:30:15,865 --> 00:30:16,945
Then you should've reminded him

505
00:30:17,025 --> 00:30:18,825
that under Clause 17 of Lime's contract,

506
00:30:18,905 --> 00:30:21,865
unauthorized personnel may not
discuss possible changes to a proposal,

507
00:30:22,625 --> 00:30:24,025
especially not after drinking.

508
00:30:24,105 --> 00:30:26,145
We only discussed public information.

509
00:30:30,385 --> 00:30:32,705
Boss, are you flying a plane?

510
00:30:32,785 --> 00:30:34,225
Keep this up,
and I'll throw up in your car.

511
00:30:34,305 --> 00:30:36,545
Then I'll pull over up ahead.
You can get a cab.

512
00:30:36,625 --> 00:30:38,065
No, don't.

513
00:30:39,065 --> 00:30:40,585
Tomorrow, forward to Legal

514
00:30:40,665 --> 00:30:43,585
all records of informal communication
with their company.

515
00:30:43,665 --> 00:30:46,545
Remember to email them a warning.

516
00:30:47,745 --> 00:30:48,945
Isn't that a bit much?

517
00:31:05,625 --> 00:31:08,585
WELCOME HOME

518
00:31:11,985 --> 00:31:13,745
FRIENDLY BASKETBALL GAME

519
00:31:19,585 --> 00:31:20,865
If that bothers you,

520
00:31:21,465 --> 00:31:23,145
we can keep our relationship private.

521
00:31:24,905 --> 00:31:26,745
What do you mean
by a private relationship?

522
00:31:30,025 --> 00:31:31,705
Dating is too much trouble.

523
00:31:31,785 --> 00:31:34,425
And I can't be bothered
to maintain a romantic relationship.

524
00:31:35,185 --> 00:31:38,665
If you're willing,
we can keep this between us.

525
00:31:39,225 --> 00:31:40,985
If it works, we continue.

526
00:31:41,065 --> 00:31:42,305
If it doesn't, we end it.

527
00:31:45,625 --> 00:31:48,105
If either of us wants to date

528
00:31:48,185 --> 00:31:50,345
or sleep with someone else,

529
00:31:50,425 --> 00:31:51,985
we tell the other person honestly

530
00:31:55,465 --> 00:31:57,385
and end what we have.

531
00:32:04,345 --> 00:32:05,185
OK.

532
00:32:08,265 --> 00:32:10,345
But we have to be exclusive.

533
00:32:48,705 --> 00:32:50,705
I'm exhausted.

534
00:32:50,785 --> 00:32:53,385
I thought once Luke got promoted,
I'd get a break,

535
00:32:53,465 --> 00:32:56,665
bBut this supplier shake-up
has me making calls all day.

536
00:32:56,745 --> 00:32:58,465
What am I, a propeller?

537
00:32:58,545 --> 00:33:00,025
Is there anything I can help with?

538
00:33:00,105 --> 00:33:01,425
Not really.

539
00:33:01,505 --> 00:33:04,185
It's because these old suppliers
keep making snide remarks,

540
00:33:04,265 --> 00:33:05,305
and it's getting on my nerves.

541
00:33:05,385 --> 00:33:06,865
Don't let it get to you.

542
00:33:06,945 --> 00:33:08,465
I'm having a little get-together tonight.

543
00:33:08,545 --> 00:33:09,825
A girls' night.

544
00:33:09,905 --> 00:33:10,985
Want to come?

545
00:33:11,065 --> 00:33:12,585
We'll have a few drinks and have some fun.

546
00:33:13,425 --> 00:33:14,585
Oh, right.

547
00:33:15,545 --> 00:33:18,425
The system says today's your birthday.

548
00:33:18,505 --> 00:33:20,585
Happy birthday, Tao.

549
00:33:20,665 --> 00:33:21,945
What do you want for your birthday?

550
00:33:23,785 --> 00:33:24,625
I want…

551
00:33:24,705 --> 00:33:26,505
How about I set you up with someone?

552
00:33:27,105 --> 00:33:30,345
He's a childhood friend of mine,
three years older than you.

553
00:33:30,865 --> 00:33:32,985
His family owns a small restaurant,
he owns three apartments,

554
00:33:33,065 --> 00:33:35,025
and he's really good-looking.

555
00:33:35,105 --> 00:33:35,945
Think about it.

556
00:33:36,025 --> 00:33:38,745
If you two start dating,
you and I can hang out all the time.

557
00:33:38,825 --> 00:33:39,665
What do you say?

558
00:33:39,745 --> 00:33:41,825
I'm not looking for a boyfriend right now.

559
00:33:42,585 --> 00:33:45,385
Then just have dinner with him

560
00:33:45,465 --> 00:33:47,465
and get to know him, OK?

561
00:33:50,945 --> 00:33:51,865
Hello?

562
00:33:51,945 --> 00:33:53,505
Mr. Wan.

563
00:33:57,465 --> 00:33:58,545
Come in.

564
00:33:59,465 --> 00:34:02,585
Boss, you really saw it coming.

565
00:34:02,665 --> 00:34:05,385
One of Wan Jun's
recommended suppliers contacted me.

566
00:34:05,465 --> 00:34:08,304
A "premium supplier"
offering a 3% monthly kickback.

567
00:34:09,425 --> 00:34:10,985
What did you say?

568
00:34:11,065 --> 00:34:12,744
If they want to make money
by doing good work,

569
00:34:12,824 --> 00:34:14,025
they can earn it honestly,

570
00:34:14,625 --> 00:34:15,985
but don't try anything under the table.

571
00:34:16,065 --> 00:34:17,065
What a joke.

572
00:34:17,145 --> 00:34:17,985
Why come to me?

573
00:34:18,065 --> 00:34:20,385
Do I look like I need the money?

574
00:34:21,784 --> 00:34:23,304
How are the revisions
to the Yueteng proposal coming along?

575
00:34:24,744 --> 00:34:25,665
Isn't it due next week?

576
00:34:26,264 --> 00:34:28,465
I want it tonight.
Next week will be too late.

577
00:34:31,025 --> 00:34:31,865
Boss,

578
00:34:32,705 --> 00:34:34,105
I know a new broom sweeps clean,

579
00:34:34,185 --> 00:34:35,865
but could you sweep a little faster?

580
00:34:35,945 --> 00:34:39,304
If you ruin my habit
of never working overtime,

581
00:34:39,385 --> 00:34:41,025
I really can't last here.

582
00:34:41,105 --> 00:34:42,865
When promotion season comes,

583
00:34:42,945 --> 00:34:45,465
with a raise, a new car, and a new bag,

584
00:34:45,545 --> 00:34:46,824
you'll find a way to keep going.

585
00:34:48,545 --> 00:34:51,065
Fine. I'll finish it tonight.

586
00:34:52,465 --> 00:34:53,385
What about Flora?

587
00:34:53,465 --> 00:34:54,784
She can help you.

588
00:34:55,625 --> 00:34:58,545
You have to let Flora
leave on time tonight.

589
00:34:58,625 --> 00:35:00,705
-Why?
-It's her birthday.

590
00:35:01,865 --> 00:35:02,705
Her birthday?

591
00:35:02,785 --> 00:35:03,945
We're having a girls' karaoke night.

592
00:35:04,025 --> 00:35:05,265
We want to have a few drinks together.

593
00:35:05,945 --> 00:35:07,145
I'll get back to the proposal.

594
00:35:07,225 --> 00:35:08,945
I can still make it in time
to cut the cake with her.

595
00:35:19,505 --> 00:35:21,225
PURE K

596
00:35:21,305 --> 00:35:23,505
I'm here, girls!

597
00:35:25,185 --> 00:35:26,865
Happy Birthday!

598
00:35:26,945 --> 00:35:28,105
-Come on.
-Thank you!

599
00:35:28,185 --> 00:35:29,385
Let's put on "Happy Birthday".

600
00:35:29,465 --> 00:35:30,945
-I'm on it.
-Thank you!

601
00:35:32,945 --> 00:35:35,145
A birthday cake!

602
00:35:35,225 --> 00:35:36,065
Come on.

603
00:35:37,705 --> 00:35:40,945
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

604
00:35:41,025 --> 00:35:44,465
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

605
00:35:45,705 --> 00:35:47,585
<i>Happy Birthday, Tao.</i>

606
00:35:47,665 --> 00:35:49,065
Happy Birthday!

607
00:35:49,145 --> 00:35:50,825
Birthday girl, say a few words.

608
00:35:52,785 --> 00:35:54,305
-Come on, say something.
-All right.

609
00:35:55,185 --> 00:35:59,105
This is my first birthday in Beijing.

610
00:35:59,185 --> 00:36:00,865
Thank you all for coming.

611
00:36:00,945 --> 00:36:03,505
I'll have many more birthdays,

612
00:36:04,025 --> 00:36:07,105
and I hope you'll be there for every one.

613
00:36:07,185 --> 00:36:08,185
-We will.
-That's all.

614
00:36:08,265 --> 00:36:09,305
I love you all.

615
00:36:09,385 --> 00:36:11,025
We love you too.

616
00:36:13,945 --> 00:36:15,465
-Come on.
-Cut the cake.

617
00:36:15,545 --> 00:36:17,025
-Hurry.
-Cut the cake.

618
00:36:17,625 --> 00:36:19,465
-Time for some cake!
-Come on.

619
00:36:19,985 --> 00:36:21,105
It's beautiful.

620
00:36:21,185 --> 00:36:23,105
Cheers!

621
00:36:36,385 --> 00:36:38,385
HAPPY BIRTHDAY, SHANG ZHITAO
FOREVER EIGHTEEN AT HEART

622
00:36:47,585 --> 00:36:49,185
Here comes the good stuff.

623
00:36:49,745 --> 00:36:50,705
Try it.

624
00:36:52,585 --> 00:36:55,825
I've seen people polish walnuts,
but never a phone.

625
00:36:56,585 --> 00:36:58,025
Keep that up, and it'll develop a patina.

626
00:36:59,305 --> 00:37:00,465
Is it really that hard to call?

627
00:37:02,265 --> 00:37:04,865
Is Ms. Shang's number too hot to handle?

628
00:37:05,745 --> 00:37:07,105
It's her birthday today.

629
00:37:09,345 --> 00:37:10,705
I see. She didn't invite you,

630
00:37:11,305 --> 00:37:12,625
so you came here to drown your sorrows.

631
00:37:16,105 --> 00:37:18,145
SHANG ZHITAO

632
00:37:27,425 --> 00:37:29,265
CAN YOU FINISH THE PROPOSAL TODAY?

633
00:37:33,105 --> 00:37:33,945
That's it?

634
00:37:38,665 --> 00:37:39,705
Luke,

635
00:37:40,665 --> 00:37:42,785
I really want to whack you
with a rolling pin from the kitchen.

636
00:37:43,865 --> 00:37:45,745
What are you thinking?

637
00:37:45,825 --> 00:37:47,945
Why is it so hard for you
to say something nice?

638
00:37:50,065 --> 00:37:52,025
Ms. Shang likes you,

639
00:37:52,105 --> 00:37:55,105
and I can tell you care about her, too.

640
00:37:55,185 --> 00:37:57,785
You two stop waiting for the other person
to make the first move.

641
00:37:57,865 --> 00:38:00,425
I know she didn't invite you
to her birthday party,

642
00:38:01,025 --> 00:38:03,545
but you still could've wished her
a happy birthday.

643
00:38:04,145 --> 00:38:05,225
Look at what you sent.

644
00:38:05,905 --> 00:38:09,865
Even a bank's birthday greeting
would sound warmer than that.

645
00:38:25,745 --> 00:38:26,585
Tao,

646
00:38:27,865 --> 00:38:30,545
-I need to leave early.
-Why?

647
00:38:31,185 --> 00:38:32,385
My landlord's taking back
the apartment tomorrow.

648
00:38:32,465 --> 00:38:34,105
I need to go back and pack.

649
00:38:34,185 --> 00:38:35,585
You're going to Hong Kong, China?

650
00:38:35,665 --> 00:38:36,825
Yes. I leave tomorrow.

651
00:38:36,905 --> 00:38:38,385
Tomorrow?

652
00:38:39,785 --> 00:38:42,825
My time in Beijing ends today.

653
00:38:46,945 --> 00:38:48,985
I haven't even had a proper talk
with you tonight.

654
00:38:49,665 --> 00:38:51,105
I'll miss you.

655
00:38:52,585 --> 00:38:54,305
Hey, it's okay.

656
00:38:54,905 --> 00:38:56,545
Friends don't have to be nearby.

657
00:38:58,385 --> 00:38:59,225
Tao,

658
00:38:59,865 --> 00:39:02,665
you'll definitely make something
of yourself in Beijing.

659
00:39:04,225 --> 00:39:08,545
Unlike you, I can't choose
between love and my career.

660
00:39:11,705 --> 00:39:14,505
Neither can I. But I understand you.

661
00:39:16,585 --> 00:39:20,785
Falling for someone
can make you feel so helpless and afraid.

662
00:39:22,265 --> 00:39:23,785
Love is an adventure.

663
00:39:24,305 --> 00:39:25,785
You can't weigh the gains and losses.

664
00:39:29,385 --> 00:39:32,065
It's fine. It'll all pass.

665
00:39:32,825 --> 00:39:33,825
We're all growing.

666
00:39:42,665 --> 00:39:43,705
Come on.

667
00:39:43,785 --> 00:39:45,225
Let me take a picture of you.

668
00:39:46,785 --> 00:39:47,665
What are you talking about?

669
00:39:47,745 --> 00:39:48,945
Love.

670
00:39:49,745 --> 00:39:52,145
We only live for around 30,000 days.

671
00:39:52,225 --> 00:39:53,345
If you like someone, tell them.

672
00:39:53,425 --> 00:39:54,665
If you miss them, go see them.

673
00:39:54,745 --> 00:39:56,745
As long as we're safe,
and it's what we want,

674
00:39:56,825 --> 00:39:57,905
we have nothing to lose.

675
00:39:57,985 --> 00:39:58,825
Exactly.

676
00:39:58,905 --> 00:40:03,505
My boss says any marriage
without dating first

677
00:40:03,585 --> 00:40:04,785
is downright indecent.

678
00:40:04,865 --> 00:40:08,025
Your boss just wants
everyone in China to sign up…

679
00:40:08,105 --> 00:40:09,945
-Exactly!
-And pay membership fees.

680
00:40:10,665 --> 00:40:14,425
-I don't get it.
-Cue up "Auld Lang Syne"!

681
00:40:14,505 --> 00:40:16,185
It's for your boss!

682
00:40:16,265 --> 00:40:17,105
OK!

683
00:40:18,825 --> 00:40:21,145
HAPPY BIRTHDAY, SHANG ZHITAO
FOREVER EIGHTEEN AT HEART

684
00:41:00,665 --> 00:41:02,105
Luke, sorry.

685
00:41:02,185 --> 00:41:03,665
I didn't hear my phone ring.

686
00:41:04,185 --> 00:41:05,305
<i>Where are you?</i>

687
00:41:05,385 --> 00:41:07,065
I'm out with some friends.

688
00:41:07,665 --> 00:41:08,585
Have you been drinking?

689
00:41:14,545 --> 00:41:15,585
Is today your birthday?

690
00:41:23,825 --> 00:41:26,305
Why do you remember my birthday?

691
00:41:28,745 --> 00:41:31,225
I know. Because as my boss,

692
00:41:31,825 --> 00:41:35,745
you have to remember
every employee's birthday.

693
00:41:35,825 --> 00:41:38,465
It's part of Lime's corporate culture.

694
00:41:39,345 --> 00:41:40,705
Any birthday wishes?

695
00:41:42,065 --> 00:41:43,185
<i>Wishes?</i>

696
00:41:44,305 --> 00:41:46,625
Will they come true if I make them?

697
00:41:47,865 --> 00:41:48,785
Tell me.

698
00:41:51,105 --> 00:41:53,225
I want…

699
00:41:55,025 --> 00:41:57,225
I want the people I love

700
00:41:58,425 --> 00:42:00,665
to stay in Beijing forever.

701
00:42:02,665 --> 00:42:04,705
And I want…

702
00:42:09,305 --> 00:42:11,625
to hold on to whatever I can.

703
00:42:13,505 --> 00:42:14,785
<i>Like my job.</i>

704
00:42:15,985 --> 00:42:18,385
And…

705
00:42:20,265 --> 00:42:22,585
I want to become a better person.

706
00:42:26,265 --> 00:42:27,265
That's all?

707
00:42:38,185 --> 00:42:40,225
I want to hold on to you too,

708
00:42:41,985 --> 00:42:43,145
Luan Nian.

709
00:44:08,665 --> 00:44:10,185
Cheers, my friends!

710
00:44:10,785 --> 00:44:11,865
Cheers!

711
00:44:24,265 --> 00:44:25,105
<i>Hello?</i>

712
00:44:26,945 --> 00:44:28,065
Where are you?

